      "position": 4,
      "section": "What I’m watching",
      "category": "video",
      "title": "The Biggest Little Farm",
      "creator": null,
      "note": "This film first caught my eye with its [beautiful trailer](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UfDTM4JxHl8). It has a 95% audience score [on Rotten Tomatoes](https://www.rottentomatoes.com/m/the_biggest_little_farm), and here’s the shortened description: “_The Biggest Little Farm_ chronicles the eight-year quest of John and Molly Chester as they trade city living for 200 acres of barren farmland and a dream to harvest in harmony with nature. Through dogged perseverance and embracing the opportunity provided by nature’s conflicts, the Chesters unlock and uncover a biodiverse design for living that exists far beyond their farm.” Their story made me reflect on life and “problems” differently.",
